<Layout title="About" active="about"><div class="document"><header class="doc-header"><p class="intro">The thinking behind the toolkit</p><h1>A skills guide,<br/>not a rulebook.</h1><p class="lede">Small, practical instructions for the moments when working with a coding agent needs more direction.</p></header><section><h2>Made by Peng Xiao</h2><p>This guide brings together skills for understanding a problem, recovering context, working through a task, and checking the result. Choose what fits your work; the catalogue is not a required sequence.</p><p>The source and complete packages live in <a href="https://github.com/MrCoder/mrcoder.github.io">the public GitHub repository</a>. The human guides explain the skills. Each package’s <code>SKILL.md</code> is the agent’s source of instructions.</p></section><section><h2>Useful habits, kept explicit</h2><p>Some skills produce diagrams or recover previous decisions. Others add a deliberate pause before implementation or a check before merging. Autonomous work has its own boundaries and setup requirements, described on the relevant skill pages.</p></section><section><h2>Sources and licences</h2><p>The original Field Guide was inspired by <a href="https://x.com/trq212/status/2073100352921215386">Thariq’s field guide to Fable</a>. This website is adapted from <a href="https://www.aihero.dev/skills">AI Hero’s skills guide</a>; the source is available in our <a href="https://github.com/MrCoder/ai-hero">AI Hero fork</a>. Our skill content and installation packages remain in the MrCoder repository.</p><p>Licences apply to individual packages where included. The history package includes an MIT licence. This site does not claim that every skill or the whole repository shares that licence. Check a package’s source before reusing it.</p></section><section><h2>Start with the task</h2><p>Browse the catalogue, read a skill’s requirements, then install its complete package.</p><a class="button" href="/">Browse the skills</a></section></div></Layout>
